line	
line	<str>Go upstairs and search the southernmost bookcase on the eastern wall for a Book on Baxtorian.</str>
line	
line	<str>Left-click Read Book on Baxtorian and close the book again, or the key will not appear for the next part.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Tree Gnome Village maze.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the dungeon at the end of the maze.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go east and search the off-coloured crate near the entrance of the room for a key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go west and open the gate ("door") with the key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Golrie, he will give you Glarial's pebble.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bank all items EXCEPT Glarial's pebble, some food and a transport method (Runes won't be allowed since you won't be able to enter the tomb if you have anything deemed "not peaceful" in your possession; Jewellery is allowed including any jewellery that has any combat bonuses. You must have at least 2 open inventory spaces).</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Glarial's Tombstone, east of the Waterfall. Use the pebble on it to enter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go west, search the chest to find Glarial's amulet. (Pick-up an extra amulet or two by dropping it from your inventory and picking them up from the ground).</str>
line	
line	<str>Return and go the other way to search the tomb to find Glarial's urn.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the bank and get 6 air runes, 6 water runes, 6 earth runes, rope, some food, Glarial's amulet, and Glarial's urn. (Warning, there are several high level monsters in the waterfall dungeon.) Weapons and armour are also allowed in the cave, so feel free to get these back too.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way back to Baxtorian falls, board the raft, use your rope on the rock (across the water to the south), then use your rope on the dead tree. DO NOT GET IN THE BARREL.</str>
line	
line	<str>Carry/equip Glarial's amulet and enter the doorway.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the right path and search the northernmost crates for a key.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go back and to the left side, avoid the fire giants, use the key on the door.</col>
